acct.blob.core.windows.net/: "`acct.blob.core.windows.net/` is not a valid Azure endpoint key: write `<host>` or `<host>/<account>`"
"127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1/": "`127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1/` is not a valid Azure endpoint key: write `<host>` or `<host>/<account>`"
proxy.internal/accta/: "`proxy.internal/accta/` is not a valid Azure endpoint key: write `<host>` or `<host>/<account>`"
acct.blob.core.windows.net/general/noarch: "`acct.blob.core.windows.net/general/noarch` is not a valid Azure endpoint key: write `<host>` or `<host>/<account>`"
proxy.internal/accta/general: "`proxy.internal/accta/general` is not a valid Azure endpoint key: write `<host>` or `<host>/<account>`"
proxy.internal/accta?sv=token: "`proxy.internal/accta?sv=token` is not a valid Azure endpoint key: write `<host>` or `<host>/<account>`"
"proxy.internal/accta#frag": "`proxy.internal/accta#frag` is not a valid Azure endpoint key: write `<host>` or `<host>/<account>`"
acct.blob.core.windows.net@evil.example: "Azure blob URL must not contain userinfo (`user:pass@host`), userinfo is invalid in blob URLs"
acct.blob.core.windows.net/../accta: "Azure blob channel URL segment `..` is a relative path segment; a channel URL must name the container it addresses directly, so write the path without `.` or `..`"
"acct.blob.core.windows.net/general\\..\\evil": "Azure blob channel URL segment `..` is a relative path segment; a channel URL must name the container it addresses directly, so write the path without `.` or `..`"
acct.blob.example//accta: "Azure blob channel URL path `//accta` has an empty segment; a doubled `/` names nothing, so write the path with single separators"
acct.blob.example/acc%zz: "Azure blob channel URL segment `acc%zz` contains `%zz`, which is not a valid percent-escape; write a literal `%` as `%25`"
"acct.blob.core.windows.net:": "`acct.blob.core.windows.net:` is not a valid Azure host: its port is empty; expected `host` or `host:port`"
acct..blob.core.windows.net: "`acct..blob.core.windows.net` is not a valid Azure host: one of its labels is empty; expected `host` or `host:port`"
"127.0.0.1:10000": "`127.0.0.1:10000` has no storage account label: a host-style key needs a dotted host whose first label is the account; write `<host>/<account>` to name the account in the path"
"[::1]:10000": "`[::1]:10000` has no storage account label: a host-style key needs a dotted host whose first label is the account; write `<host>/<account>` to name the account in the path"
localhost: "`localhost` has no storage account label: a host-style key needs a dotted host whose first label is the account; write `<host>/<account>` to name the account in the path"
localhost.: "`localhost` has no storage account label: a host-style key needs a dotted host whose first label is the account; write `<host>/<account>` to name the account in the path"
"azurite:10000": "`azurite:10000` has no storage account label: a host-style key needs a dotted host whose first label is the account; write `<host>/<account>` to name the account in the path"
"--as-user.blob.core.windows.net": "`--as-user` is not a valid Azure storage account name: account names are 3-24 characters of lowercase letters and digits only"
acct-1.blob.example: "`acct-1` is not a valid Azure storage account name: account names are 3-24 characters of lowercase letters and digits only"
